  "description": "BAVNAP crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H94 Mn5 N9 O32 Tm5 2+,2(Cl1 1-),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tm1 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm2 (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Tm3 (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Tm1C (Tm) has 7 O neighbors; Tm2C (Tm) has 8 O neighbors; Mn2C (Mn) has 4 O neighbors; Mn3C (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.107-4.068 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 93.87-123.66°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H94Cl2Mn5N9O32Tm5·2MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
